    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16516" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ē-vulgo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">evolgo</span></b> ), āvi, ātum,
		1, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to bring out among the people</i>, <i>to publish</i>, <i>divulge</i> (not ante-Aug.,
			and very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">civile jus repositum in penetralibus pontificum
					evulgavit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 9,
					46</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arcanum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. H.
					1, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">injurias,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. A.
					13, 19</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pudorem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 14, 14</span></i>
			.—With an <i>object-sentence</i> in
			direct discourse: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sic evulgari jussit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					13, 9</span></i>
			.</div>
